That's certainly creative thinking, however I wouldn't necessarily call it
safer. When you teleport a monster, it can randomly reappear anywhere on
the level, including very near where it started, e.g. almost next to you.
One of the main survival rules in Nethack is to never be burdened, where
being strained or stressed as above will allow the monsters to get many
turns to each of yours. Sam is very very fast to begin with, so there's a
decent chance doing this will result in him running up and decapitating you
before you can get outside.

